+/* A join is the point joined at, the ends of the two sides on the outside of the turn, and the tip of the mitre
+ * between them, twice: once from each side, so that the vertex shader can cut it off square at the mitre limit,
+ * sliding each back along its own side.  Bevelled, both come back to the same point; within the limit they are the
+ * same point already.  Where the stroke turns straight back, the join is whatever the stroke style makes reach
+ * ahead of the point: a rectangle, as long as the mitre limit or, for a round join, half the width. */
